 ("Reverse Repo Rate", "The rate at which the RBI borrows money from commercial banks against government securities, absorbing excess liquidity.", "When banks have surplus cash, they park it with the RBI and earn this rate.", "", "Used to drain liquidity; since 2022 the Standing Deposit Facility is the effective floor of the corridor.", "Repo Rate, SDF, LAF", ""),
 ("CRR (Cash Reserve Ratio)", "The share of a bank's Net Demand and Time Liabilities (NDTL) that it must keep as cash with the RBI. Banks earn no interest on it.", "With a 4% CRR, a bank with Rs 100 crore NDTL keeps Rs 4 crore with the RBI.", "CRR amount = CRR % x NDTL", "A higher CRR reduces the money banks can lend, so it tightens liquidity.", "SLR, NDTL, LAF", ""),
 ("SLR (Statutory Liquidity Ratio)", "The share of NDTL that banks must hold in liquid assets (cash, gold, approved government securities) with themselves.", "A bank with Rs 100 crore NDTL and an 18% SLR must hold Rs 18 crore in liquid assets.", "SLR amount = SLR % x NDTL", "Ensures banks stay solvent and creates demand for government bonds.", "CRR, NDTL, MSF", ""),
 ("MSF (Marginal Standing Facility)", "A window where scheduled banks borrow overnight funds from the RBI against government securities, by dipping into their SLR holdings, at a rate above the repo rate.", "A bank short of cash at day end borrows under the MSF instead of defaulting.", "", "Emergency borrowing; its rate is the upper end of the policy corridor.", "Repo Rate, SLR, Bank Rate", ""),
 ("Bank Rate", "The rate at which the RBI lends long-term funds to commercial banks; a penal rate that is aligned with the MSF rate.", "Used as a benchmark for penalties on banks that fall short of reserve requirements.", "", "Frequently asked in exams as a policy rate other than repo.", "MSF, Repo Rate", ""),
 ("SDF (Standing Deposit Facility)", "A facility where banks park surplus funds with the RBI overnight without giving collateral. Introduced in April 2022; it forms the lower end of the policy corridor.", "A bank with idle cash deposits it with the RBI under the SDF.", "", "Replaced reverse repo as the effective floor of the corridor.", "Reverse Repo, LAF, Repo Rate", ""),
 ("LAF (Liquidity Adjustment Facility)", "The RBI's tool to inject or absorb short-term liquidity daily through repo and reverse repo style operations.", "The RBI injects liquidity via repo auctions when money is tight.", "", "The core day-to-day liquidity management tool.", "Repo Rate, SDF, MSF", ""),
